which comedy legend's crotch jokes  inspired melissa roush's career keep  watching to discover how this talented  performer landed her big break as  bernadette on the big bang theory when  melissa roush made her first appearance  as howard's blind date bernadette on  cbs's the big bang theory in 2009 it  didn't seem likely she'd be coming back  the pair hardly hit it off with howard  offering crude jokes and questions about  her interests and bernadette  indifferently swatting each one away but  then at dinner they suddenly bonded over  their meddling mothers a spark was  kindled and a recurring role was born  shocked viewers realized the graceless  howard had finally found his perfect  match and the romance which would lead  to marriage in season 5 came as a  surprise to roush 2 telling backstage  magazine i was so grateful when big bang  happened i was supposed to be a one-time  guest star landing a hit series was a  major accomplishment for the  up-and-coming actress but it didn't  happen overnight roush was just a kid  when she got hooked on comedy that's  when she started working toward her  chosen career and began developing the  character that would one day get her a  big break as bernadette hey  it's a good thing you did that you would  have regretted it your whole life your  whole life feels good don't it feels  good from her first awkward car ride  with howard roush created a character  that set bernadette apart as smart cute  and quick-witted but if there's one  trait fans can't forget about her it's  her chirpy childish voice which she  modeled after her mother rausch told  insider my mother sounds very similar to  bernadette she's got a very high pitched  voice except with a new jersey accent  and i grew up imitating her roush also  mimicked stars she saw on tv like whoopi  goldberg and don knotts it was a great  way to overcome her natural shyness at  school but it didn't always work out as  planned telling roger ebert.com i would  memorize stand-up sets that weren't my  own which i didn't realize was not  allowed since i was seven years old they  were actually really inappropriate for a  kid my age in one instance roush  memorized a set from a whoopi goldberg  hbo special that had a lot of f-bombs  the teacher ended up calling roush's mom  about how roush went from being shy and  barely talking one minute to using very  inappropriate language the next whoopi  goldberg had this character where she  was like pointing at her crotch and  being like over here as roush got older  her interest in performing comedy and  getting on stage grew stronger she also  found more appropriate outlets to  express herself she spent most of her  free time doing community theater  attending theater camp and making up  shows in her basement with her brother  ben raised jewish it made sense that  roush even had a comedy club themed bat  mitzvah when she was a young teen roush  couldn't remember a time when she didn't  want to be an actress throughout her  childhood the adults around her  supported and guided her toward her  dreams telling inside jersey i went to  brookdale arts camp for my entire  childhood and had a fantastic theater  counselor there who gave me some of my  first comedic sketches to do i also had  a terrific theater teacher at marlboro  high school who taught me a great deal  and was very encouraging without that  support she might not have taken the  next steps toward her future success  after graduating high school roush went  to marymount manhattan college to study  acting she encountered great teachers  there and one in particular helped her  with voice work so her new jersey accent  wouldn't be quite so strong others  taught her how to build on her natural  ability to create characters but roush  knew she had to do even more to grow as  a performer by that point she'd realized  that comedians write their own material  so she began performing her stand-up  sets in new york city clubs telling  roger ebert.com i did stand up for about  10 years in new york and i was one of  those comedians who started out just  handing out flyers on the street in the  freezing cold to get people to come see  comedy in order to get stage time i  would love to eventually go back to it i  grew up being such a huge fan of comedy  and stand-up as if she wasn't working  hard enough roush also started writing  with college friend winston bygoal who  she met freshman year beigel came to  watch her set and they decided to write  some sketches together because they had  a very similar sensibility and their  favorite thing to do was make each other  laugh but even with all that training  and effort her professional career  seemed stuck in neutral after she'd  graduated telling inside jersey i don't  think people knew what to do with me i'd  have people say maybe i should dye my  hair lose weight gain weight it was  never a specific box you could check it  was just yeah sorry not my cup of tea  and of course i was really green too i'd  go out for parts in cargo pants and a  jean jacket without any makeup roush did  land some gigs and she was excited to be  part of the vh1 series best week ever  but she needed her big break roush  already knew how to write a stand-up set  so she started writing solo shows  wherever she could from burger joints to  laundromats telling inside jersey just  knowing i could do that at night made it  easier waiting tables all day she was  still riding with beigel who she was  dating and would soon marry when they  got the idea to write a one-woman show  together it started as a not very funny  autobiographical story about trying to  make it after college but then they were  inspired by jenna bush hagar who was  around rausch's age and about to start  teaching at a charter school rausch told  interview magazine so we decided to  combine the two the one woman show that  we were writing for me with this idea of  making it through jenna bush's voice and  exploring the bush presidency through  her eyes we called it the miseducation  of jenna bush and it was a way to do  this coming of age story a young woman  coming into her adulthood while also  using the bush presidency for some  comedic exploration the show was a hit  it earned awards at comedy festivals and  roush's performance caught the eye of an  agent the time seemed right to move to  la even then though roush had to hit  rock bottom before she could finally  rise to the top of her game telling  entertainment tonight i was at the  unemployment office the day before i got  the audition for the big bang theory i  was doing a lot of driving around crying  in my car i was just in that out-of-work  actor grind thankfully roush nailed the  audition and wound up with much more  than a guest spot after a lifetime of  dreaming and working she'd secured her  spot in hollywood  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite big bang theory stars are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

